# Evidence integrity

Keep evidence classes distinct. Never upgrade one into another:

historical · replay · backtest · simulation · shadow · prospective forward
test · paper · live

Never overwrite failed observations, insert later-known data, rewrite
timestamps, fabricate missing evidence, or rerun and substitute results while
preserving the original label.

Missing or ambiguous evidence stays explicit (`UNKNOWN`, `PENDING`, `STALE`,
`UNAVAILABLE`, `NOT_OBSERVED`, or the platform's existing canonical token).
Do not coerce a gap into a passing result.

No AI development task may enable or place live real-money trades.
`LIVE-001` remains blocked. Any move from simulation/paper toward live
execution requires explicit governed authorization.

RTH / FTEP / scheduler / prospective runs: inspect only unless the task
explicitly authorizes mutation. Do not restart, relabel, or "fix" active
evidence collection.

Audit workflow: skill `imp-evidence-integrity`.
